<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Motor Guard — top-down car placeholder, tuned to the Diagnostics hotspot anchors
  in TopDownCarRenderer.kt (x% = fraction of intrinsic 200dp width, y% = fraction
  of intrinsic 420dp height; FRONT IS UP).

  ══ HOW TO SWAP IN YOUR OWN ART ══
  1. Drop a PNG (transparent background recommended, ideally ≥2× pixel size of
     200×420dp — e.g. 400×840px) into this folder as e.g. `car_topdown.png`
     beside this file, then DELETE this `car_topdown.xml` (same name can't exist
     twice), or give yours a distinct name (`car_topdown_v2.png`).
  2. Anchor coordinates live in TopDownCarRenderer.kt. If your art has a different
     aspect ratio than 200×420 (~1:2.1), edit the `x`/`y` fractions of each
     HotspotAnchor there to match where components actually sit in your image.
     The zoom animation compensates automatically for aspect differences (the
     anchors are fractions, not pixels), but eyeballing the dot positions against
     your art is still required for a polished result.
  3. Keep FRONT UP in your art — the rest of the surface (and docs) assume it.
-->
